	)
	(text "- VDD (pin 10) from VSYS with C501 1 uF; pin 6 VDD/NC tied to VDD as the datasheet allows.\n- REG (pin 1): internal 1.8 V regulator output, C502 1 uF required.\n- EN (pin 5) <- HAPT_EN (P2.05). IN/TRIG (pin 4) <- HAPT_TRIG (P1.10, PWM20 OUT0).\n- SDA/SCL on the shared bus; VIH = 1.3 V, so 1.8 V logic is fine. I2C address 0x5A.\n- OUT+ (7) / OUT- (9) to the LRA lead pads TP501 (LRA+) and TP502 (LRA-), 1.0 x 1.5 mm, hand-soldered.\n- MECHANICAL: the 9 mm LRA tape-down pad is a layout feature (bare area on an FR4 stiffener on island B),\n  not a schematic part. Motor: Vybronics VG0832012, taped with its own adhesive backing.\n- DO NOT switch the driver's VDD off: SDA, SCL, EN and IN/TRIG are limited to VDD + 0.3 V, so an unpowered\n  DRV2605L would be back-powered through its I2C pins and clamp the shared bus. Rev A keeps VDD on with EN low\n  (about 4 uA). Firmware blocks the motor while VBUS is present (VSYS then follows VBUS up to 5.5 V,\n  above the 5.2 V recommended maximum; abs max is 5.5 V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 147.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "0b237a68-40cb-4b35-99fe-53b70877043d")
	)
	(text "Haptics sheet (step 5): TI DRV2605L (VSSOP-10, DGS) on VSYS, I2C at 1.8 V. From TI datasheet SLOS854D."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 15.24 0)
		(effects
